<Layout title="How we rate songs | MelodyMeter"><article class="text-page"><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CLARITY</p><h1>Higher score. Easier melody.</h1><p>MelodyMeter rates the ease of singing a song’s recognizable main lead melody in a comfortable key. A score of 10 is easiest. You don’t need to copy the original singer’s tone, optional ad-libs, or layered backing vocals.</p><h2>AI gets the conversation started</h2><p>AI ratings are provisional judgments from available song information and the model’s learned knowledge. Audio has not been analyzed. We don’t present exact tempo, note range, or timing measurements without supporting evidence. Unfamiliar songs may remain unrated.</p><div class="guide-factors">{FACTORS.map(f => <div class="guide-factor"><strong>{f.label} · {f.weight}%</strong><p>{f.description}</p></div>)}</div><p>The AI overall score is the rounded weighted average of these nine factors. Scores 1–2 are very hard, 3–4 hard, 5–6 medium, 7–8 easy, and 9–10 very easy.</p><h2>The audience takes the lead after 10 ratings</h2><p>Once 10 different verified emails have submitted an overall rating for a song/version, the audience average becomes the main score. We show that average to one decimal place and retain the AI estimate separately.</p><p>Each individual factor also needs 10 audience ratings before its audience score qualifies. The audience overall average uses people’s overall scores, independently of the optional factor scores.</p><h2>Your experience counts once per song</h2><p>Anyone can rate. Submit an overall score, optionally rate the factors you understand, and verify your email. Opening the email link shows your scores; pressing Confirm rating counts the vote. Updating a rating replaces your earlier vote.</p><h2>A useful starting point</h2><p>Community ratings describe the experiences of the people who voted. Your voice, familiarity with the song, and chosen key can change how comfortable it feels. Choose a key that fits your voice and practice at a comfortable volume.</p><h2>Installing and using offline</h2><p>Use Install app when offered by your browser. On iPhone, open this site in Safari, tap Share, and choose Add to Home Screen. Sign in with Google to sync saved songs across devices. Visited and saved songs can be read offline. Submitting votes and generating new estimates requires a connection.</p></article></Layout>
